# Every file in which the fork is allowed to differ from upstream: the files
# it adds, and the files of upstream's that it changes. A name that ends in
# a slash is a directory, all of which is the fork's.
#
# The proof reports any other file that differs from the pinned upstream
# commit.
#
# None of upstream's own test files is listed, so the proof reports it if one
# of them differs. The tests that the fork adds beside upstream's are in
# files of their own, most of them named *_fork_test.go. Upstream's tests are
# upstream's expectations, and a fork that has to change one to pass it has
# changed what it does.
#
# Adding a line is a decision for a person. See proposals/workflows.
